  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Three statements about Boltzmann’s constant k<sub>B</sub> are:</p>\n<p>I.   k<sub>B</sub> has a unit of J K<sup>−1</sup></p>\n<p>II.  k<sub>B</sub> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"=\\frac{\\textit{gas constant}}{\\textit{Avogadro’s constant}}\"></span></p>\n<p>III. k<sub>B</sub> <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"=\\frac{\\textit{the average kinetic energy of particles}}{\\textit{temperature of the gas}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Which statements are correct?</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">I and II only</li><li data-label=\"B\">I and III only</li><li data-label=\"C\">II and III only</li><li data-label=\"D\">I, II and III</li></ol>"
  },
